Chapter: PitRate

 Core 0's PIT runs at 1,193,182 / 11,932 = 99.998 Hz, and the operands
 separate that exact rate from a rounded one: a day is 8,639,869 whole ticks
 where 100 Hz gives 8,640,000 and 18.2 Hz 1,572,480. 164, 54 and 219 ms are
 the waits `GopXhci` and `MicInput` ask for.

Section: Body

  ms-ticks : Integer -> Integer
  ms-ticks (ms) = (ms * pit-input-hz + pit-count * 1000 - 1) / (pit-count * 1000)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (if pit-input-hz == 1193182 then "the input clock is 1193182 hz" else "INPUT CLOCK " & show pit-input-hz)
    print-line-uni (if pit-count == 11932 then "the count is 11932" else "COUNT " & show pit-count)
    print-line-uni ("164 ms is " & show (ms-ticks 164) & " ticks")
    print-line-uni ("54 ms is " & show (ms-ticks 54) & " ticks")
    print-line-uni ("219 ms is " & show (ms-ticks 219) & " ticks")
    print-line-uni ("a day is " & show ((86400 * pit-input-hz) / pit-count) & " ticks")
  end
